      "description": "OneNote\n\nOneNote is a Microsoft Office product that focuses on providing its consumers with a comprehensive, digital note-taking solution.  Here are some highlights of my work in the services (backend) space for this product:\n\n- Maintained publicly available OneNote REST APIs, with a focus on authentication, authorization, and production reliability.\n- Designed and implemented modular C# auth middleware used by my team and two partner teams, replacing tightly coupled auth classes with shared components enabled through environment settings.\n- Enabled independent, parallel microservice migrations through per-service rollout controls; collaborated with three sister teams across the broader auth initiative.\n- Built parallel validation of legacy and new auth using caller-identity parity checks and dashboards. Used telemetry to promote new auth from non-enforcing to primary, supporting rollouts with minimal customer impact.\n- Built inbound and outbound auth regression tests, using mocks to verify expected user information across success and failure scenarios.\n- Improved incident mitigation time by standardizing reliability and requests-per-second dashboards and troubleshooting guides linking alerts, mitigation steps, and contacts; migrated legacy alerting to support finer-grained tuning.\n- Explained the auth architecture and supplied evidence during privacy and security reviews.\n- Served as a diversity and inclusion driver by organizing team activities and events.\n- Co-organized annual volunteering events.",
      "insights": ""
     },
     {
